        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add follow-up task suggestions",
        "body": "Closes #102421\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nModels can identify valuable follow-up coding work, but they previously had no operator-approved way to turn that recommendation into a fresh, isolated coding session. Plain-text suggestions are not actionable, while starting a subagent immediately skips consent and does not create a user-owned managed-worktree session.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds configurable `spawn_task` and `dismiss_task` model tools to the coding tool group. A proposal becomes an ephemeral Control UI card and never starts automatically; accepting it creates a new seeded session in its own managed worktree. The gateway owns a bounded, permission-checked lifecycle, and worktree-backed sessions consistently reuse their persisted worktree path for agent runs, replies, compaction, and sandbox reporting.\n\nSuggestions are intentionally process-local. Acceptance is task-ID-only and idempotent, uses the server-stored prompt and project root, and rolls back partial session/worktree creation before restoring a retryable suggestion.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can inspect, accept, or dismiss model-recommended follow-up work without interrupting the current turn. Accepted work opens as a fresh coding session with the exact proposed prompt and an isolated managed worktree. Administrators can configure both tools through the existing tool policy, coding profile, and tool groups.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Full changed-surface gate passed on Blacksmith Testbox: `pnpm check:changed` — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28991563745\n- Focused gateway, agent-tool, worktree, sandbox, compaction, protocol, and UI suites passed; the final focused batches covered 547 assertions, with 35/35 Control UI browser cases.\n- Core production and test `tsgo` lanes passed.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check` and `pnpm check:protocol-coverage` passed.\n- Generated Swift protocol models matched the official generator byte-for-byte; native protocol guards passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh autoreview completed with no accepted or actionable findings.\n\nAI assistance: Codex implemented and reviewed the change; the product contract was maintainer-provided and all reported evidence was run against the resulting patch.\n",
